==>MVC 
 The Model-View-Controller (MVC) architectural pattern separates an application into three main components.
    .Model => Class Represent Table In Database 
    .View  => Html Page 
    .Controller => Project Controller
           .Class Inherit From Class (Controller)
           .Its Name Must End With Model-View-Controller
           .Contain Public Non-Static Functions Called Actions 
           .Have 5 Actions [CRUD Operations] => GetAll , GetbyId , Update , Delete , Add

